   "description": "Morning on the boat. Lunch under the pines in the french riviera. Dinner late, in a suit, somewhere worth dressing for. One watch made for all of it. Inside is the Seiko VK64, one of the most trusted hybrid chronograph movements made today. Quartz precision with the snap of a mechanical chronograph hand. You feel it every time you press the pusher. The chronograph itself carries history. Invented in 1816 for astronomy, sharpened a century later with the tachymeter, and carried into aviation, racing, and naval navigation. You wear all of that on your wrist. Polished stainless case. Roman numerals at twelve and six. On the tip of second hand there is the orange color that catches the light like the late afternoon sun on the Côte d'Azur. Turn it over and you'll find a sailboat engraved into the case back, inspired by the ones anchored off the french riviera on any given afternoon",
